        "execSummary":  "The ATLAS data is the most strategically useful Google release this week: it shows that AI productivity gains are real but unevenly distributed, and that workflow redesign—not just tool access—is the bottleneck. The finding that scientists save seven hours weekly but still face validation constraints maps directly to a problem enterprise AI leaders face: adoption without process re-engineering produces marginal gains. Regional variation signals that global enterprises need localized AI adoption strategies, not one-size-fits-all rollouts. The data is Google-curated and reflects Google\u0027s tool ecosystem, so independent longitudinal studies should be sought for strategic planning.",
