        "execSummary":  "This is one of the most consequential AI governance documents of 2026: Anthropic is disclosing that AI now leads 26% of its own research work—up from under 1% in February—and proposing standardized metrics for the entire frontier AI industry to adopt. For enterprise AI leaders, the key implication is that AI self-improvement is already operational at the lab level, and the pace is accelerating faster than most enterprise governance frameworks assume. The oversight figures (blocking only 0.002% of agent actions) suggest that current monitoring is calibrated for low false-positive rates, not adversarial robustness. Any enterprise deploying autonomous AI agents should treat these lab-level metrics as a leading indicator of what their own governance frameworks will need to handle within 12-24 months.",
